# Project plan HTML

`index.html` is the living project plan. Keep it single-file (CSS/JS inline) unless the user asks to split it.

## Structure to preserve

- Hero: brand **Bonsai** dominant, one headline, one short support line, CTA group, full-bleed plant photo.
- Lead with **named projects** (goal, material, success criteria), then **Phase 0 / start-now** for the current month, then reference care (calendar, soil, prune, train, fertilise).
- When adding plants, add a new named project (or extend an existing one) — do not leave species only as vague groups.

## Design constraints

- Expressive fonts (already Syne + Figtree); avoid Inter/Roboto/Arial defaults.
- Atmospheric background; no purple-gradient AI look, no emoji decoration, no card grids in the hero.
- Mobile-readable tables and lists; checklist may use localStorage.

## Content tone

- Practical and Melbourne-specific. Prefer actionable steps and months over theory.
- Label uncertain IDs clearly; never invent certainty.
